Lara's feedback is solid. I'll bake her two adjustments into the implementation:

1. Component confidence levels — Instead of binary "component/not component", each detected
component will include:

```json
  {
   "selector": "div.cta",
   "confidence": "high",
   "frameCount": 10,
   "totalFrames": 10,
   "coverage": 1.0
  }
```

- high: appears in 60%+ of frames
- medium: appears in 30-59%
- low: appears in 10-29%
- Below 10%: not included

This way the AI (and human) know which components are structural patterns vs. one-off elements.

2. Color role disambiguation — When multiple saturated colors exist, the extractor will:
- List all saturated colors sorted by frequency
- Assign --color-accent-1, --color-accent-2 (deterministic, not arbitrary)
- Include a note: "Multiple saturated colors detected. Human should assign semantic names." in the
  output
- Not force a single "accent" pick

3. Phase 4 stays deferred. Agreed. No shared CSS injection this sprint.

